spes scaler: accept IOSurfaceAcceleratorSetCustomFilter (selector 4) from stage 2 (0228).

all-14 and all-21: CollectionsPoster (and once assetsd) call selector 4 with a 32-byte struct and nothing out; the stand-in
answered kIOReturnUnsupported ("not done", 24 logged, the limit of the log). Disassembly of IOSurfaceAccelerator.framework
(20H392, local): _IOSurfaceAcceleratorSetCustomFilter -> IOConnectCallStructMethod(conn, 4, block, 0x20, NULL, NULL); block =
u32 ratio (0x8000 = 1.0), u32, u32 table dimensions, the same three again, u64 address of the coefficients in the caller;
callers: Portrait, CMImaging, CMCapture, QuartzCore copy_iosurface (ignores the result), SetFilterCoefficients.
The software scaler has no filter (nearest pixel), so the request is checked, logged (12 lines, own counter) and answered
with success; the coefficients are not read. Quality may differ from a filtered scale. Whether CollectionsPoster's
"extension check-in timeout" has to do with it is not known. Not run on hardware yet.

